<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Annama Deva</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Annama Deva is the traditional founder of the Kakatiya royal line of Bastar in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. According to tradition he was a brother of the last Kakatiya king Prataparudra and fled north after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warangal">Warangal</a> in 1323. The goddess <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danteshwari">Danteshwari</a>, said to have accompanied him, became the patron deity of the Bastar rulers.</p></div>
